      "requirement": "A tabulated n,k table is axis data of the core: Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs EpsAxisDispersion gains TabulatedNK of TabulatedNkTable, a [<NumericCarrier>] record of ascending wavelengths in metres, n and k arrays and the one-case interpolation rule TabulatedInterpolation (LinearInWaveLengthClamped, wire tag 1, tryOfWire). TabulatedNkTable.tryCreate refuses an empty table, unequal columns and a decreasing wavelength column with typed TabulatedTableError cases. Its complexIndex is buildTabulatedClosure's arithmetic moved verbatim: each sample at its own wavelength, linear in wavelength between neighbours, clamped to the first and last samples, and a one-sample table constant. OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs entryFromTabulated builds that table for a refractiveindex.info tabulated page and for an n,k CSV, and carries it as Some complexity: one isotropic dispersive segment over the table's own sample range, view-only (isEditable false), with properties = complexity.toProperties. buildTabulatedClosure is deleted, and formula imports are untouched. A tabulated axis has the facet key 'Tabulated n/k'. No number moves: the imported eps equals the old closure's at every sample and every midpoint. Proved red first (the import's complexity is None), then green.",
